**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**How to implement.** Before a second preset store exists, the preset store's refusal gets a case of its own and a member both stores call (AGENTS.md 'Reuse, never copy', 'Error DUs carry diagnostic payload'; .spec-md §4 'Errors and IO'). `LibraryUnavailableErr` (`ElementId.fs:LibraryError`) says the Library could not be read, yet the in-memory preset store (`ElementId.fs:LibraryEntryStore`, built by the `createInMemory` that step 58 renamed) answers it for an id it already holds, as 'the only fitting existing case'. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ElementId.fs`: `LibraryError` gains `PresetRefusedErr of reason : string`, the preset store refused an entry, and `LibraryUnavailableErr`'s doc says the store beneath the proxy failed. Directly after `LibraryError`, `type LibraryError with static member entryAlreadyHeld (entry : LibraryEntry) : LibraryError` answers `PresetRefusedErr` with today's text (`library entry '<id>' is already present`), and the in-memory store's `addEntry` calls it; its doc is one line citing spec 0050 S2.3. The `LibraryEntryStore` and builder docs say a duplicate is `PresetRefusedErr`. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs`: the library reason (step 37), the one complete match on `LibraryError`, gains the case, so an import's refused preset still answers `ImportRejectedErr` with the same reason. Any other complete match on `LibraryError` the build reports gains it the same way. (3) Tests. `LibraryProxyTests` gains `the preset store serves an added preset by kind and by id, and refuses an id it already holds`: over `Library.createInMemory ()`, `addEntry` of `BuiltinCatalogue.preset` of `PresetIds.detectorIntensity`, `PresetIds.polarizerLp` and `PresetIds.source600` each answers `Ok ()`; `entriesForKind` answers exactly the detector for `Detector`, the polarizer for `LinearPolarizer` and the source for `LightSource`; `tryGetEntry` answers each for its id and `Ok None` for a fresh `newSourceId ()`; and a second `addEntry` of the detector answers `Error (PresetRefusedErr reason)` whose reason names its id, after which `entriesForKind Detector` still answers the one detector.

**Acceptance.** After the case lands, `ElementId.fs` MUST declare `PresetRefusedErr` on `LibraryError` and `LibraryError.entryAlreadyHeld`, which the in-memory preset store calls; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the preset store serves an added preset by kind and by id, and refuses an id it already holds`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the eleven s10 invariants MUST pass.
